Q9.14
question: What must pass before Core freezes?
options: four checked representative proofs / prose inventory / full-language soundness first
reason: Check reset generativity/dependencies, deferred allocator/loan cleanup, heap opening/mutable lending and one values-to-bytes lemma; return substantive formalization discoveries to A2.
rec: Provisional approval, then four kernel-checked theorems against a proposed Spec.lean, then freeze
agree: Y
revises: No
note: R4 F8. The four: reset_fresh (a reset gives a brand distinct from every live one), defer_cleanup_releases (structured exits run deferred destroy/give_up in reverse and release loans), open_mut_freezes_root (a mutable heap borrow blocks all other root access), rep_roundtrip (slice-1 types encode/decode). The sequence itself is row Q9.19. reset_fresh also proves that resets in a loop give pairwise-distinct brands and that old-brand values are refused by the new allocator's operations. defer_cleanup_releases covers every structured exit, releases each held loan after its call, and preserves the allocator-dependency check. open_mut_freezes_root also proves a shared open never grants writes. rep_roundtrip covers u8–u64, bool and the empty struct.
upd: True
